(LST-11 — append onto a mixed list respects the appended element's own
 type.
 Also covers: LST-12 (`set element N of` retypes a slot in place),
 LST-13 (`element N of` reads each slot back as its own type),
 LST-14 (`'s first` / `'s last` respect the slot type),
 LST-16 (the VARIABLE form of `{...}` interpolation, in PRINT position,
 renders the whole list with each element as its own type).
 Ran: VOX_CORE_PATH=/home/josj/scr/english/vox/coreasm /home/josj/scr/english/vox/target/release/vox LST-11.vox -o p && ./p
 expected output:
   appended
   retyped
   two
   3.5
   retyped
   appended
   interp: ["retyped", "two", 3.5, 1, "appended"]
   ["retyped", "two", 3.5, 1, "appended"]
)
a list called mixedbag is [1, "two", 3.5, yes].
append "appended" to mixedbag.
print element 5 of mixedbag.
set element 1 of mixedbag to "retyped".
print element 1 of mixedbag.
print element 2 of mixedbag.
print element 3 of mixedbag.
print mixedbag's first.
print mixedbag's last.
print "interp: {mixedbag}".
print mixedbag.
